Z||000018||Uaana||04-02-2001||04:08 PM||||Well I'm out. That new SE I picked up is going to eat the funds I was planning on using for the trip.<BR>BTW Standard what was it that broke on your GT steering right after you got it? This thing likes to wander all over the road, was it the ball joints or wheel bearings?<BR>How do you know if you have bad ones?||||reg||1
Z||000019||Standard||04-03-2001||09:52 AM||||I had a bad lower ball joint, and one of the uppers went not too long after.  To see if the ball joints are bad, jack up the front of the car, grab the wheel at the 12 & 6 o'clock position and rock it back and forth.  There shouldn't be any play.  If there is, get a helper and have them rock the wheel while you look to see where it's coming from.  If the car has anywhere near 100,000 miles and everything still looks original there's a good chance the ball joints should be replaced.  <P>Replacing the lower b/j's is a pain.  Uppers are a piece of cake...<P>Could also be worn-out tie rods and/or tie rod end-links.  I'm pretty sure mine are gone but don't know how to check them.<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
